WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.037
<v Avery>Security news. Here&#x27;s what CISA flagged this week.

00:00:04.257 --> 00:00:08.801
<v Avery>Seven vulnerabilities joined the known exploited list in the last seven days.

00:00:09.181 --> 00:00:20.445
<v Cole>On the list: WordPress Core, Ivanti Connect Secure, GitLab Community Edition, Cisco Secure Firewall ASA Software, and Broadcom VMware ESX.

00:00:20.665 --> 00:00:22.372
<v Cole>Plus one more on screen.

00:00:22.752 --> 00:00:26.741
<v Avery>If any of those are in your environment, your exposure desk will call it out.

00:00:27.121 --> 00:00:42.695
<v Cole>Cloudflare Zero Wire has five briefings marked needs attention: Linux IPv4 TCP use-after-free, php2shell, eMudhra certificate compromise, node2shell, and Citrix NetScaler command execution.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:53.421
<v Avery>Those are public briefings, not findings on our network. Open the news desk for the sources and patch guidance. Matching open findings get context on their action cards.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:01:04.105
<v Cole>Cloudflare coverage is a compensating control. It does not replace the vendor patch or a rescan, and we have not verified coverage for this environment.
